---
title: "publishSaleResults (LegionFixedPriceSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_caller: Legion operator publishes results
    q_check_caller --> q_check_timing: caller is Legion operator
    q_check_caller --> q_revert_auth: unauthorized caller
    q_check_timing --> q_check_not_published: block.timestamp >= refundEndTime
    q_check_timing --> q_revert_timing: refund period not ended
    q_check_not_published --> q_set_merkle: results not yet published
    q_check_not_published --> q_revert_published: results already published
    q_set_merkle --> q_set_tokens: claimMerkleRoot = _claimMerkleRoot, acceptedCapitalMerkleRoot = _acceptedCapitalMerkleRoot
    q_set_tokens --> q_set_config: totalTokensAllocated = _totalTokensAllocated
    q_set_config --> q_emit: tokenDecimals = _tokenDecimals
    q_emit --> [*]: emit SaleResultsPublished(claimMerkleRoot, totalTokensAllocated)
    q_revert_auth --> [*]: revert Unauthorized
    q_revert_timing --> [*]: revert RefundPeriodNotEnded
    q_revert_published --> [*]: revert AlreadyPublished

    note right of q_set_merkle
        INV-001: Merkle roots are immutable once published
        INV-002: Results can only be published after refund period ends
        INV-003: totalTokensAllocated must match sum of all individual allocations in Merkle tree
    end note
